title = Taiyaki
description = Taiyaki is a Japanese fish-shaped cake, commonly sold as street food. It imitates the shape of tai , which it is named after. The most common filling is anko. Some shops even sell taiyaki with okonomiyaki, gyoza filling, or a sausage inside. Smaller, differently shaped versions called kingyoyaki are also available and often sold in bags of five, ten, or more.
